<div class="article-detail-page">
    <div class="article-body">

        <p>Ready to start selling? Submitting your seller application only takes a few minutes, and most sellers get access right away.</p>
        <p>This guide covers who can apply and how to complete your application in the app.</p>

        <hr />

        <h2>Before you apply</h2>

        <h3>Check eligibility</h3>
        <p>Most sellers can apply as long as they meet these requirements:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>You live in a <a href="#">country where selling on Lively is supported</a></li>
            <li>You're at least 13 years old</li>
        </ul>

        <p>If you're 13–17, you'll need a parent or guardian's permission and must complete a special application.</p>
        <p><a href="#">Learn more about teens on Lively.</a></p>

        <h3>Selling in gated categories</h3>

        <p>A small number of categories require additional approval after you're granted seller access, such as Luxury Bags &amp; Accessories and Wholesale. <a href="#">Please refer to this article</a> for a complete list of gated categories and selling formats.</p>
        <p>If you plan to sell in one of these categories, you will need to submit additional information to be reviewed by the Lively team.</p>
        <p>To apply to sell in a gated category:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>On the app:</strong> Go to the <strong>Seller Hub</strong> &gt; menu icon in top right corner &gt; <strong>Seller Status</strong> under Settings &gt; scroll to <strong>Gated Categories</strong> &gt; <strong>Apply Now</strong> &gt; fill out form</li>
        </ul>

        <p><a href="#">Learn more about selling in gated categories.</a></p>

        <h2>Complete your seller application</h2>

        <h3>1. Start your seller application</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>Open the Lively app.</li>
            <li>Tap on the profile icon at the bottom of the screen and apply as a seller.</li>
            <li>Tap Get Started.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>You'll answer a short series of questions about your experience and selling plans.</p>

        <h3>2. Agree To Lively's Guidelines</h3>
        <p>Review and agree to our <a href="#">Community Guidelines</a> to help keep Lively safe and fun for everyone.</p>

        <h3>3. Choose your primary seller category</h3>
        <p>You'll next answer a few short questions about your selling history.</p>
        <p>Whether you're brand new or already selling elsewhere, choose the options that best describe your experience level. This helps us understand how to support you.</p>

        <h3>4. Tell us about your selling experience</h3>
        <p>We'll start with a few quick questions about your selling business. Select the option that best describes your experience level. Whether you're brand new or already selling elsewhere, just choose what fits best.</p>
        <p>This helps us understand how to support you.</p>

        <h3>5. Enter your return address</h3>
        <p>Enter your full legal name exactly as it appears on your government-issued ID.</p>
        <p>Enter the address you will be fulfilling orders from. We will use this to calculate how much the buyer pays in shipping costs, which may be partially determined by the distance between the return address you submit and the buyer's address.</p>
        <p>After you're approved, you can <a href="#">update your name and return address</a> in Seller Hub if you prefer to use a business name or alias. You may also use a PO Box, as long as the name field contains at least 2 characters.</p>

        <h3>6. Submit your application</h3>
        <p>In most cases, you'll unlock seller access within minutes. If additional review is needed, we'll notify you with next steps (check your email).</p>
        <p>Once approved, follow the in-app checklist to schedule your first show.</p>
        <p>Need more help? <a asp-action="StartSelling">Learn how to start selling on Lively.</a></p>

        <div class="helpful-widget">
            <p>Was this article helpful?</p>
            <div class="helpful-buttons">
                <button type="button">Yes</button>
                <button type="button">No</button>
            </div>
            <span>80 out of 145 found this helpful</span>
        </div>

    </div>
</div>